  "id": "Compound::DB00388 - Gene::146",
  "verbalization": "Phenylephrine, a selective alpha-1 adrenergic receptor agonist, is implicated in the relationship with Adra1d through a series of mechanistic pathways. The evidence suggests that Phenylephrine binds to Adra1a and Adra1b, which are both involved in the activation of Alpha1-adrenergic receptors. These receptors, in turn, are part of a broader pathway that leads to the participation of Adra1d. The scores from the paths indicate a consistent and significant relationship, with Phenylephrine interacting with Adra1d through a shared pathway involving Alpha-adrenergic receptor activity. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Phenylephrine may influence Adra1d, though the exact role of Adra1d in this context remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a direct interaction between Phenylephrine and Adra1d through the activation of alpha-1 adrenergic receptors, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise functional role of Adra1d in this process.",
